tains 35 film contrast  55 classic film colors together with the  beloved resolution effects  as you can see i already created a  couple clips with these power grades and  they look really really good  first in the color tab left corner make  a couple power grade albums by pressing  right click and choose add power grade  album  make four of them and rename them by  double clicking on the album name first  will be the note 3 second film contrast  third film color and the last will be  the halation  you can find the power grade on my  website link in description down below  go into each folder and start importing  the creative film pack one by one by  pressing right click and import with  output lut  [Music]  now that we have everything imported and  organized let me show you how to use the  creative film powergrade and how you can  make your own custom film luts  [Music]  you can start by either adding your own  nodes pressing alt s on windows or  command s on mac or by using my custom  node tree to save you some time i'll use  the already imported node tree to make  it easier let's add a contrast and  exposure to establish the base look of  the footage so you can understand  exactly what i'm doing nodes are pretty  much just like layers in photoshop and  they work sequential meaning the last  node always will have power over the  rest so if i add a final node and lower  down the saturation it will affect all  the other nodes this is a quick tip you  can enroll in my online classes if you  want to learn more tips about color  grading in a short period of time link  in description so first we set a  contrast and exposure to see what we are  working with scrub to all the film  contrast to see exactly how it will  affect the image and then choose your  favorite  to apply it just drag and drop on top of  the node we can go in the curve tab and  adjust it to your liking you're gonna do  this with regular luts which is a huge  advantage if you don't like the one  chosen and you want different film  contrast hit control z on windows or  command z on mac to reset the node to a  previous version then just choose a new  film contrast and apply it  [Music]  remember you must activate the splines  to edit the curve  [Music]  next we scroll through the classic film  color album and check a couple to see  which one would best fit our footage  again you just have to drag and drop on  top of the desired node  i'll just apply a couple to see how it  affects image until i find one that i  like  to switch between the film colors faster  i just drag and drop the film color then  hit ctrl z to reset the note 3 to  previous versions and apply a new film  color from here you either leave it as  it is or you can dive deeper into the  settings and adjust different values  i have a node explanation sheet  contained in the product folder so you  know exactly how each node affects the  image and where are the adjustments  located  as you can see there are some really  great color palettes in this collection  and it's making my life so much easier  from here you can either leave it as it  is or you can dive deeper into the  settings and adjust different values  in the film color node you can go into  different curves tabs and adjust the  colors on your taste  for example in this shot i feel like the  reds are too saturated so i will just go  into huber's saturation and bring it  down just a notch  so this is much faster and easier than  starting from scratch with a regular  grade and you have full control compared  to a classical lot  if you're using davinci you can play  around with inhalation settings and  you're pretty much done if you're a  premiere or final cut user follow the  next steps to export the lot  right click on the clip and choose  generate lut remember lust contain only  three values hue saturation and luma so  any davinci resolve plug-in effects  won't be contained by the lut so let's  disable the collision and the film grain  let's make a 65 point q blot to ensure  colors will not fall apart  choose the destination folder and export  and now you can create as many luts as  you want without even having to learn  color theory  you can also create black and white lots  just bring down the saturation to zero  and apply your favorite film contrast  this is how you can easily create your  own lots using the creative film power  grade for davinci resolve there's a link  to the power grade in the description  down below  the cool part about this power grade is  compatible with the rest of my product  let's say we have a super 8 mm home film  power grade you haven't seen the video  i'll put a link in the upright corner  for you to watch later all you have to  do is just choose a clip and double  click to apply the power grade it's that  easy  let's adjust the contrast to match the  footage and here you can see multiple  nodes all our names so it's easier to  find and know what you're working with  these power grades were made to work  with any kind of footage log rec709  10-bit or even 8-bit it's finely tuned  so colors won't fall apart  this power grade pack comes in 10  flavors and has really vibrant and  nostalgic kind of colors but even though  you have 10 different flavors maybe you  get bored and just want something new so  you can borrow a color palette from the  creative film power grades and create  something completely new go back to the  classic film color album and just drag  one of the color schemes onto the film  color node and now you have a totally  different look and this applies with all  my power grades the 35 read and film the  8 millimeter home film and the vhs  camcorder emulation which is a huge  value if you think about it  so what i'm trying to do with these  power grades is give you great color out  of the box but also give you full  control over how the image should look  like and also enable you to be more  creative  combining 35 contrast gammas together  with over 50 classic film colors your  possibilities are pretty much limitless  and can easily get over 1000 unique lot  variations and that without even  entering the notes and modifying them  so you can find all these power grades  on my website the major problem with  using luts they sometimes don't work  well with our footage because it was  shot in different scenarios with  different lightings and colors  so if the footage is a little bit  overexposed or has different colors then  you just start working against a lot to  match it with the rest of the footage  and end up spending more time repairing  something that could have been only a  couple of minutes because luts are  destructive while power grades are not  now you can take control of your image  by creating your own custom lots easily  without any compromises with power  grades you can easily edit with full  control you can actually learn about  color theory just by going inside each  node and experimenting with a good base  finally if you don't want to use davinci  you just export the desired look as lots  and you can use them in premiere pro  final cut or any other editing software  but davinci is free and has great color  grading features and the experience is  much nicer  if you want to find out more about color  grading i invite you to my online course  which will help you easily understand  color grading in a short period of time  in this course i will guide you in the  process of creating your own footage and  explain different techniques that will  make the whole process easier to grasp  all the lots will be provided at the end  of the course for free so go check it  out save your spot is going to be fun  link in description so that's it for  today hope this helped clear out some  questions let me know in the comments  what you like to see next until then  have fun and stay curious  see ya  [Music]  you

